{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when men strive.</b> Why is this stated? Since it says 'וכי יזיד איש,' we have heard only about one who intends to strike his enemy and strikes him — that he is liable to death; but one who intends to strike his enemy and strikes his friend — we have not heard. Scripture states: 'וכי ינצו אנשים.' And there are those who interpret it for monetary law, and this is what it says: since it says 'ואיש כי יכה כל נפש אדם,' I might think even an eight-month-old [fetus] is included; Scripture states: 'וכי ינצו אנשים' — he is not liable unless he kills a viable child." "<b>A pregnant woman.</b> Why is this stated? For when it says <b>וגו׳ ויצאו ילדיה</b>, we have learned that she is pregnant. Rather, to teach you that if he struck her on her head or on one of her limbs, he is not liable unless he struck her in the place of her fetus. Another interpretation: to hold him liable even for a single child." "<b>ענוש יענש.</b> Rashi explained: the value of the offspring. And if you ask: why is he not executed for these offspring that he killed? And if you say: perhaps they were nonviable — if so, it would be difficult for you regarding anyone who kills a person — why is he executed? Perhaps he killed a טרפה! And one may answer: we rely on the majority, and the majority are not טרפה, as we say in chapter 1 of Hullin. So too we should rely on the majority, that most women do not miscarry. If so, he should be liable to death for striking the woman! Rather, one may answer: he is not liable for any creature until it has emerged into the air of the world, as is proven in tractate Arakhin." "<b>As the husband of the woman shall lay upon him.</b> If he reaches a settlement with him. And if not — 'ונתן בפלילים' (and he shall give through judges): an example would be a pearl mixed with oil and its weapon."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:37.068611248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}